    "created_at": "2020-11-11T13:12:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-11T13:12:57Z",
    "body": "> Why can `_blank` not be used?\r\n\r\nIn an ideal world it could, but in practice iOS has piloted to open `_blank` in the in-app browser, which caused Chrome to reflect this behavior. See comments 3 and 4 of the [more context](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=709889#c3) link.\r\n\r\n> (Note that `_blank` already implies `noopener`\r\n\r\nYes, and finally [in Chrome 88](https://www.chromestatus.com/feature/6140064063029248), too.\r\n\r\n> ([A]nd note that `noopener` is redundant if you specify `noreferrer`).)\r\n\r\nRight. It's probably some browser compatibility thing or tooling ([maybe VS Code](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/50709625/link-with-target-blank-and-rel-noopener-noreferrer-still-vulnerable#comment113302839_50709724)?) that they get used redundantly. \r\n",
